## Errors & Mistakes
- In the very first version, no test covered the null path of prefill
  capacity_classes. Removing the attribute hid that gap instead of
  fixing it; the review brought the attribute back with tests.
- The earlier lifecycle test used PlanOnly steps for change and removal
  to avoid rolloutStartGracePeriod, so no test applied an update with
  Pd. The review found this.
- golangci-lint thelper flagged SetRolloutStartGracePeriod without
  t.Helper(); fixed.

## Attempts & Outcomes
- Applying update steps with the 30 s grace period would have raised
  the package test time from about 9 s to about 70 s. Making the period
  a test-overridable var was chosen instead.
- The first version of the lifecycle test had a same-config plan-only
  step and state checks that repeat what terraform-plugin-testing
  already checks after every apply step. They stay removed.
- Moving TestDeploymentPDLifecycle into deployment_hotload_test.go was
  refuted earlier: test files in coreweave/inference are named for the
  tests they hold.

## Findings & Constraints
- The pinned buf.build/gen/go/coreweave/inference module
  (v1.36.12-20261008185853-22f8f31f8962.2) already has DeploymentPD and
  DeploymentPDPoolAutoscaling.capacity_classes. It has no autoscaling
  claims field.
- The API message cannot tell an empty repeated list from an unset
  one. A list attribute therefore needs the prior model value to keep
  a configured null.
- terraform-plugin-testing v1.16.0 runs a non-refresh plan and a
  refresh plan after every apply step and fails when either is not
  empty.
- proto.Equal treats two nil typed messages as equal, which the removal
  step relies on.

